<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <!--
      docs/plan/03 § Providers — the fifth project: "the shared provider conformance suite,
      parameterised".

      ⚠ IT CONTAINS NO ASSERTIONS, AND IT IS THE TWELFTH FAMILY TO TEST THAT CLAIM — TWICE OVER SINCE
      #32. The workspace added a new KIND of resource: one whose objects are configuration for a data
      plane rather than a description of a workload. The alert rule added a new SHAPE: a clusterless
      child under a cluster-backed parent, read through an IConvergedModule while its ancestor is
      converged against the fake cluster in the same run. test/CyberCloud.Conformance still needed no
      change for either.

      ⚠ THIS PROJECT IS ONE OF THE SUITES THE Labels ARCHITECTURE GATE COUNTS. Build.Architecture
      § LabelsGate runs EveryAppliedObjectCarriesTheSevenMandatoryLabelsAndBothAnnotations in every
      *.Conformance project under src/Providers — for the workspace it asserts the seven labels on
      three objects; for the alert rule it asserts there is no object at all.

      ⚠ IT REFERENCES A PROJECT UNDER test/, which docs/plan/03 § test/ intends: CyberCloud.Conformance
      is "the shared provider suite (parameterised, REFERENCED BY PROVIDERS)". docs/plan/03 § Assembly
      graph rules is about the shipped graph and excludes test projects by construction.

      ⚠ AND CyberCloud.Communication's IMPLEMENTATION, since #32, for the reason the sending module's own
      conformance project references it: the alert evaluator grain takes an IMessageSender, so the
      harness silo has to host the sending module the way the silo host does — MonitorAlertingModule
      calls AddCyberCloudCommunication. No carrier is registered and nothing in the suite sends.
    -->

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Shouldly"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup Label="Global usings">
        <Using Include="Xunit"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="../CyberCloud.Providers.Monitor/CyberCloud.Providers.Monitor.csproj"/>
        <ProjectReference Include="../../../CyberCloud.Communication/CyberCloud.Communication.csproj"/>
        <ProjectReference Include="../../../../test/CyberCloud.Conformance/CyberCloud.Conformance.csproj"/>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
